  "created": "2026-11-09T01:13:44.657Z",
  "description": "ADO.NET data provider for Visual FoxPro / dBase tables and database containers, built on CrossVault.FoxDbf. Use FoxPro/dBase data from Dapper, raw ADO.NET, reporting, and LINQPad via SQL: FoxDbfConnection / FoxDbfCommand / FoxDbfDataReader / FoxDbfParameter / FoxDbfConnectionStringBuilder / FoxDbfProviderFactory, plus FoxDbfDataSource (the modern DbDataSource factory for DI) and FoxDbfBatch (DbBatch). Connection string mirrors the VFP OLE DB Provider (Data Source = .dbc | directory | .dbf; Collate; Exclusive; Deleted; Ansi; ReadOnly; Accelerator=Highlike; EnforceRules/EnforceRI). Supports SELECT (INNER/LEFT/RIGHT/FULL JOIN, UNION, correlated subqueries, GROUP BY, aggregates, ORDER BY, TOP, INTO CURSOR/TABLE/ARRAY), INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE (incl. INSERT FROM ARRAY/MEMVAR and SELECT INTO ARRAY landing in the connection's active data session with _TALLY), CREATE/ALTER/DROP TABLE, the VFP work-area model (USE/SELECT), positional ? and named @/: parameters, real transactions (atomic rollback), DataAdapter/CommandBuilder, GetSchema metadata, and a static DBF-header type map. Runs a .dbc's stored procedures / UDFs via CommandType.StoredProcedure (and ad-hoc \"?expr\"/\"=expr\" evaluation) on the embedded microVFP interpreter; with the opt-in EnforceRules (alias EnforceRI) connection keyword and a .dbc open, INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE run the full VFP write model (field DEFAULTs, then field RULEs, NOT NULL/type/width, the record RULE, unique/candidate/primary-key, and finally the bound RI trigger) atomically — exactly like VFP9 (default OFF = raw DML, byte-for-byte unchanged). Output is byte-compatible with the real Visual FoxPro 9 runtime.",
  "id": "CrossVault.FoxDbf.Data",
